For further exploration, consider these books (in order):

Flow: The Psychology of Optimal Experience by Mihaly Csikszentmihalyi. This is the classic foundation of flow theory, detailing what flow feels like and how to cultivate it in life.

Curious: The Desire to Know and Why Your Future Depends On It by Ian Leslie. A thorough look at the science and stories of curiosity, explaining how to rekindle a curious mindset.

Deep Work: Rules for Focused Success in a Distracted World by Cal Newport. This book offers practical rules for building concentration and avoiding distractions, helping readers structure their work to more consistently reach flow.
